<body>
    <h1>Use Case 2.1.6.8: Admin Configures Campaign Schedule for Creates Ca=
mpaign Setup (Step-8)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an <strong>Admin</strong>, I want to set the schedule and frequency f=
or delivering phishing emails in a campaign, including choosing the deliver=
y method, campaign frequency, and expiration date, so that the campaign ema=
ils are delivered according to the planned timeline and frequency.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>In <strong>Step 8</strong> of the campaign setup, the <strong>Admin</str=
ong> configures the <strong>Schedule &amp; Frequency</strong> for the phish=
ing simulation campaign. The <strong>Admin</strong> can specify:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Phishing Delivery Method</strong> (e.g., instant, scheduled, or =
schedule later),</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Frequency</strong> (one-off, weekly, monthly, or quarte=
rly),</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong> (defines when the campaign will au=
tomatically end).</p></li>
</ul>
<p>The <strong>Admin</strong> can also choose whether to deliver the first =
batch of phishing emails immediately or schedule them for later. Additional=
ly, the <strong>Admin</strong> has the option to send a <strong>Test Email<=
/strong> to verify the configuration before finalizing the campaign. This s=
tep ensures the correct timing and delivery configuration for the campaign.=
</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Selects the delivery method, campaign frequency,=
 expiry date, and test email configuration.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays available options for delivery method,=
 frequency, expiry date, and test email functionality. Verifies and confirm=
s the settings.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> is logged in and has completed previous =
steps in the Create New Campaign wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system is operational and can display the&nbsp;<strong>Schedule &amp=
; Frequency</strong> settings for the campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> has selected a Mail Server in Step 4.</p=
></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The campaign&nbsp;<strong>schedule and frequency settings</strong> are s=
aved and ready for the next steps in the campaign creation process.</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>The system will automatically trigger the first batch of phishing emails=
 based on the specified schedule and frequency.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Set Phishing Delivery Method</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>System presents the&nbsp;Admin with the option to select the&nbs=
p;Phishing Delivery Method.</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Options:&nbsp;Immediate Delivery,&nbsp;Scheduled Delivery, or&nb=
sp;Schedule Later.</strong></p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> selects&nbsp;<strong>Scheduled Delivery<=
/strong> to specify the exact time and date of email delivery.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>If&nbsp;<strong>Immediate Delivery</strong> is selected, emails are deli=
vered as soon as the campaign is activated.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>When&nbsp;<strong>Scheduled Delivery</strong> is selected, the system re=
quires the&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> to set:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>First Batch Delivery Date</strong>: The specific date and time f=
or the first batch of phishing emails.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong>: The date when the campaign should=
 automatically end.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> selects&nbsp;<strong>Weekly Campaign Fre=
quency</strong>.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong> calculates and enforces the minimum required&nbs=
p;<strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong> (7 days from the&nbsp;<strong>First=
 Batch Delivery Date</strong>).</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> sets the&nbsp;<strong>First Batch Delive=
ry Date</strong> to &nbsp;<strong>December 01, 2025</strong>.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong> records the start date and displays it.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> sets the&nbsp;<strong>Campaign Expiry Da=
te</strong> to&nbsp;<strong>January 15, 2026</strong>.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong> validates that the date is after the minimum req=
uired expiry date (<strong>December 08, 2025</strong>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong> records and displays the selected&nbsp;<strong>C=
ampaign Expiry Date</strong>.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System enforces rules for other frequencies:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Weekly:&nbsp;Start Date + 7 days minimum.</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Monthly:&nbsp;Start Date + 1 calendar month minimum.</strong></p=
></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Quarterly:&nbsp;Start Date + 3 calendar months minimum.</strong>=
</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 2: Configure Campaign Frequency</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>System prompts the&nbsp;Admin to select the&nbsp;Campaign Freque=
ncy.</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Available options:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>One-off: Campaign will be delivered once.</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Weekly: Campaign will be delivered every week.</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Monthly: Campaign will be delivered every month.</strong></p></l=
i>
<li>
<p><strong>Quarterly: Campaign will be delivered every three months.</stron=
g></p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> selects&nbsp;<strong>Weekly</strong> as =
the campaign frequency.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System displays the selected frequency next to the&nbsp;Campaign=
 Frequency field.</strong></p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 3: Set Campaign Expiry Date</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>System prompts the&nbsp;Admin to select the&nbsp;Campaign Expiry=
 Date.</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>The&nbsp;Admin clicks the&nbsp;Pick an expiry date button to cho=
ose the expiry date.</strong></p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> selects the&nbsp;<strong>Campaign Expiry=
 Date</strong> of&nbsp;<strong>January 15, 2026</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System displays the selected&nbsp;Campaign Expiry Date below the=
 field.</strong></p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 4: First Batch Delivery Configuration</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> can select whether the&nbsp;<strong>Firs=
t Batch Delivery</strong> will be&nbsp;<strong>Scheduled</strong> or&nbsp;<=
strong>Immediate</strong>.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>If the&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> chooses&nbsp;<strong>Scheduled Delive=
ry</strong>, the system displays the selected&nbsp;<strong>First Batch Deli=
very Date</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If the&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> chooses&nbsp;<strong>Immediate Delive=
ry</strong>, the first batch of emails is sent immediately after the campai=
gn is activated.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 5: Test Email Delivery</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> can check the box labeled&nbsp;<strong>T=
est Email Delivery</strong> to send a test email and verify the campaign co=
nfiguration.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> enters a&nbsp;<strong>Test Email Address=
</strong> (e.g., "<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"mailto:your.email@comp=
any.com" rel=3D"nofollow">your.email@company.com</a>").</p></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> clicks&nbsp;<strong>Send Test Email</str=
ong> to receive the test message and ensure the campaign setup is correct.<=
/p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 6: Save &amp; Continue</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>After configuring the&nbsp;<strong>Delivery Method</strong>,&nbsp;<stron=
g>Campaign Frequency</strong>, &nbsp;<strong>Expiry Date</strong>, and&nbsp=
;<strong>First Batch Delivery</strong>, and optionally testing the email de=
livery, the&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> clicks&nbsp;<strong>Save &amp; Cont=
inue</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System validates the inputs and confirms the settings.</strong><=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> is directed to the next step in the camp=
aign setup process.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Frequency Field</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> must select=
 a frequency (One-off, Weekly, Monthly, Quarterly).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a valid campaign frequenc=
y."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is optional.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: If an expiry date is selected, it must be a=
 valid future date.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a valid campaign expiry d=
ate."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Test Email Address</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is optional.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: If a test email address is entered, it must=
 be a valid email format.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please enter a valid email address for =
the test."</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Business Rules</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"755bb61d-9382-44ec-b660-c61=
d443c138a" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Rule</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-1</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Admin</strong> must select a <strong>Campaign Frequency</str=
ong> before proceeding to the next step.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-2</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Test Email Delivery</strong> is optional but recommended to ensu=
re correct configuration.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-3</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong> is optional but must be a future d=
ate if selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-4</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>First Batch Delivery</strong> can be scheduled or sent immediate=
ly, based on <strong>Admin=E2=80=99s</strong> selection.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"13beefaf-672d-4b26-97e3-e63=
72a4c4e7c" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Pass/Fail Condition</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-01</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can select a <strong>Phishing Delivery Method</st=
rong> (Immediate or Scheduled).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Delivery method is selectable and works as expected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-02</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can select the <strong>Campaign Frequency</strong=
> (One-off, Weekly, Monthly, Quarterly).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Frequency options are available and can be selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-03</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can select a <strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong=
> (optional).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Expiry date can be selected and displayed correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-04</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can configure the <strong>First Batch Delivery</s=
trong> option, choosing between scheduled or immediate delivery.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>First batch delivery option works correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-05</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can enter a <strong>Test Email Address</strong> a=
nd send a test email.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Test email is sent successfully.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-06</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can select the <strong>Scheduled Delivery date an=
d time</strong> for emails.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Scheduled date and time are validated and displayed.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-07</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system validates that all required fields (Delivery Method, Frequenc=
y) are completed before enabling the "Save &amp; Continue" button.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>"Save &amp; Continue" button is only enabled after completing required f=
ields.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-08</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can preview the scheduled campaign delivery in a =
confirmation message before finalizing.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Confirmation message is displayed with campaign details.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-09</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can send a <strong>Test Email</strong> to verify =
the campaign configuration.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Test email is received and matches the campaign setup.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-10</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can choose to <strong>Send Test Email</strong> be=
fore finalizing campaign setup.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Test email functionality works properly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-11</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Campaign Frequency</strong> setting persists after saving.</=
p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Frequency setting remains saved and is available on subsequent views.</p=
></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-12</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can view the <strong>Expiry Date</strong> setting=
 and edit it if necessary.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Expiry date can be viewed and edited as needed.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-13</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>First Batch Delivery</strong> can be set for a specific time and=
 date.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can choose to set the first batch delivery time a=
nd date.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-14</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Campaign Settings</strong> are saved successfully after clicking=
 <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong>.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Settings are saved and confirmed by the system.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-15</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can set the <strong>Campaign Frequency</strong> t=
o "One-off" for a single delivery.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>"One-off" option functions correctly for single campaign delivery.</p></=
td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-16</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Test Email Delivery</strong> field is visible but optional.<=
/p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can choose to enable or skip test email delivery.=
</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-17</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can <strong>Edit</strong> the <strong>Campaign Fr=
equency</strong> after the initial selection.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Frequency field is editable and changes are saved correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-18</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong> can be removed if not needed.<=
/p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Expiry date can be cleared if not required.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-19</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> receives a confirmation notification when setting=
s are successfully saved.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Confirmation message is displayed after successful save.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-20</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can view the <strong>Campaign Frequency</strong> =
and <strong>Expiry Date</strong> settings in the campaign summary.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Frequency and expiry date settings are displayed in the summary.</p></td=
>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>System Behavior &amp; Validation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Schedule and Frequency</strong>:&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> mus=
t select the campaign's&nbsp;<strong>delivery method</strong>,&nbsp;<strong=
>frequency</strong>, and&nbsp;<strong>expiration date</strong> before proce=
eding.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Test Email</strong>: The system allows the&nbsp;<strong>Admin</s=
trong> to verify the campaign configuration via a test email before sending=
 the actual campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: Fields like&nbsp;<strong>Campaign Frequency=
</strong> and&nbsp;<strong>First Batch Delivery</strong> are validated to e=
nsure correct data input.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Security Handling</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Access Control</strong>: Only authorized users (<strong>admins</=
strong>) can configure campaign settings and schedule delivery.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Data Security</strong>: All campaign schedule and configuration =
data are securely stored.</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an Admin, I want to set the schedule and frequency for delivering phi=
shing emails in a campaign, including choosing the delivery method, campaig=
n frequency, and expiration date, so that the campaign emails are delivered=
 according to the planned timeline and frequency.</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>In Step 7 of the campaign setup, the Admin configures the <strong>Schedu=
le &amp; Frequency</strong> for the phishing simulation campaign. The Admin=
 can specify the <strong>Phishing Delivery Method</strong> (such as instant=
 or scheduled delivery), set the <strong>Campaign Frequency</strong> (one-o=
ff, weekly, monthly, or quarterly), and define the <strong>Campaign Expiry =
Date</strong>. The Admin can also select whether to deliver the first batch=
 of phishing emails immediately or schedule it for later. Additionally, the=
 Admin has the option to send a <strong>Test Email</strong> to verify the c=
onfiguration before starting the campaign. This step ensures the correct ti=
ming and delivery configuration for the campaign.</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Selects the delivery method, campaign frequency,=
 expiry date, and test email configuration.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays available options for delivery method,=
 frequency, expiry date, and test email functionality. Verifies and confirm=
s the settings.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin is logged in and has completed previous steps in the <strong>C=
reate New Campaign</strong> wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system is operational and can display the <strong>Schedule &amp; Fre=
quency</strong> settings for the campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin has selected a <strong>Mail Server</strong> in Step 4.</p></li=
>
</ol>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The campaign schedule and frequency settings are saved and ready for the=
 next steps in the campaign creation process.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system will automatically trigger the first batch of phishing emails=
 based on the specified schedule and frequency.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Set Phishing Delivery Method</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin is presented with the option to select the <strong>Phishing De=
livery Method</strong>.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Options include <strong>Immediate Delivery</strong> or <strong>Scheduled=
 Delivery </strong>or <strong>Schedule Later</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects <strong>Scheduled Delivery</strong> to specify the exa=
ct time and date of email delivery.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If <strong>Immediate Delivery</strong> is selected, emails are delivered=
 as soon as the campaign is activated.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Selecting <strong>Scheduled Delivery</strong> <strong>must</strong> mand=
ate setting the First Batch Delivery Date and Campaign Expiry Date.</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>Admin selects the <strong>Weekly</strong> Campaign Frequency option. Sys=
tem calculates and enforces the minimum required Expiry Date (7 days from t=
he First Batch Date).</p></li>
<li>
<p>Admin clicks to set the <strong>First Batch Delivery Date</strong> and s=
ets it to <strong>December 01, 2025</strong>.System records the start date =
and displays it.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Admin clicks to set the <strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong> and select=
s <strong>January 15, 2026</strong>.System validates that the date is after=
 the minimum required expiry date (Dec 08, 2025). System records and displa=
ys the date.</p></li>
<li>
<p>When a frequency is selected, the system <strong>must</strong> calculate=
 and enforce a <strong>minimum Campaign Expiry Date</strong> based on the c=
hosen First Batch Delivery Date:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Weekly:</strong> Start Date + 7 days minimum.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Monthly:</strong> Start Date + 1 calendar month minimum.</p></li=
>
<li>
<p><strong>Quarterly:</strong> Start Date + 3 calendar months minimum.</p><=
/li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>If <strong>Scheduled Delivery</strong> is chosen, the Admin <strong>must=
</strong> configure the specific date and time for the <strong>First Batch =
Delivery</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The <strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong> selection <strong>must</strong=
> prevent the Admin from choosing a date that falls before the enforced min=
imum expiry date</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 2: Configure Campaign Frequency</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin is prompted to select the <strong>Campaign Frequency</strong>.=
</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The available options are:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>One-off</strong>: Campaign will be delivered once.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Weekly</strong>: Campaign will be delivered every week.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Monthly</strong>: Campaign will be delivered every month.</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p><strong>Quarterly</strong>: Campaign will be delivered every three month=
s.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects <strong>Weekly</strong> for the campaign frequency.</p=
></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the frequency next to the <strong>Campaign Frequency=
</strong> field.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 3: Set Campaign Expiry Date</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin can specify the <strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong> by click=
ing the <strong>Pick an expiry date</strong> button.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the date when the campaign should automatically end.</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the selected <strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong> b=
elow the field.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 4: First Batch Delivery Configuration</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin can select whether the <strong>First Batch Delivery</strong> w=
ill be scheduled or not.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If the Admin chooses <strong>Scheduled Delivery</strong>, The system dis=
plays the selected <strong>First Batch Delivery Date</strong> below the fie=
ld.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If <strong>Immediate Delivery</strong> is selected, the first batch is s=
ent as soon as the campaign starts.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 5: Test Email Delivery</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin can check the box labeled <strong>Test Email Delivery</strong>=
 to send a test email to verify the campaign configuration.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin enters a <strong>Test Email Address</strong> (e.g., "<a class=
=3D"external-link" href=3D"mailto:your.email@company.com" rel=3D"nofollow">=
your.email@company.com</a>").</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks <strong>Send Test Email</strong> to receive a test mess=
age and ensure the campaign setup is correct.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 6: Save &amp; Continue</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>After configuring the <strong>Delivery Method</strong>, <strong>Campaign=
 Frequency</strong>, <strong>Expiry Date</strong>, and <strong>First Batch =
Delivery</strong>, and optionally testing the email delivery, the Admin cli=
cks <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system validates the inputs and confirms the settings.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin is directed to the next step in the campaign setup process.</p=
></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Frequency Field</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin must select a frequency (One-off, Weekly, Monthly, Quarterly).=
</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a valid campaign frequenc=
y."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is optional.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>If an expiry date is selected, it must be a valid date in the future.</p=
></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a valid campaign expiry d=
ate."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Test Email Address</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is optional.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>If a test email address is entered, it must be a valid email format.</p>=
</li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please enter a valid email address for =
the test."</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
